  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Community Resilience; harnessing traditional Ecological knowledge to combat climate change</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a three year project, where JHC is seeking to  enhance Voice and Agency of local community in policy dialogue that will lead to understanding impacts of climate change to marginalised and indigenous communities. Specifically, JHC is keen on how Local voices and local content developed to inform training and evidence based advocacy activities as well as  Inclusion of indigenous knowledge and information in local, national and regional policy dialogue and advocacy engagements 
Year 1 JHC carried out research on &quot;Indigenous People and Climate Change &#x2013; Fostering Indigenous food systems findings.&quot; JHC strongly assert the need for a conversation around food systems with a focus and or entry point on indigenous seeds. The project aims to draw the attention of small holder farmer communities and other stakeholders to the implications of the new seed laws and in practise help in preservation of indigenous seeds through community seed banks.    
This project will contribute to Kenya Uganda Resilience programme; 
Outcome 3: Degraded landscapes are restored and provide a stream of ecosystems services;
 Outcome 4: Women and youth influence change through voice, action, and civil society engagement and 
Outcome 5: Decision makers formulate and implement policy, plans and initiatives that support food security, natural resource management and livelihoods of women and youth. .

Intention is to  include traditional ecological knowledge as a voice of the local community into climate research, ecological education, resource planning and decision-making processes that should eventually be incorporated, as a local voice &amp; local content into the climate change policy, climate action plans and assessments, and more important for resilience improve adaptation efforts at County, National, and Regional, levels.</narrative>
  </description>
